 "notes": "TASEH CD102 haloscope, AxionPhoton g_agamma 95% C.L. exclusion. Traced the red central limit curve from Fig.2 (raster PNG Figure2.png; no ancillary data). x-axis frequency 4.70750-4.79815 GHz converted to mass via m_a=h f/c^2 (m_eV=4.13567e-15*f_Hz), giving 19.469-19.841 ueV, matching the papers stated 19.4687-19.8436 ueV. y-axis in 1e-14 GeV^-1. Per pixel column (~57 kHz, aggregating ~10 of the 5 kHz bins) the deepest (bottom-most) red pixel was taken, then binned to 90 points. Extracted g ranges ~5.3e-8.3e-14 GeV^-1; paper quotes lowest 5.3e-14, average 8.2e-14, highest 8.9e-14 GeV^-1 (binned-min slightly under-samples the 8.9 upper bins). Assumes axions = 100% of local DM at rho=0.45 GeV/cm^3. No limits placed at 4.71017-4.71019 and ~4.74738 GHz (candidate/interference regions); left in the trace as they are negligible and within factor-2 of neighbours.",
